        "original_id": "e439f5d0-65cd-550d-95e0-03ea3605208c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D. W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery, Eric Garcia\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance, Matchstick Men\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, collaborator, mentor\n- Topics: film career milestones, literary adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915 as a collaborator of D. W. Griffith.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in Intolerance in 1916.\n- Elmer Clifton gave up acting in 1917 to concentrate on work behind the camera, with D. W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery as his mentors.\n- Ridley Scott had his commercial breakthrough with Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott directed Blade Runner in 1982.\n- Matchstick Men is a 2003 British-American black comedy crime film directed by Ridley Scott.\n- Matchstick Men was based on Eric Garcia's 2002 novel of the same name.\n- Gladiator, directed by Ridley Scott, was released in 2000 and won the Best Picture Oscar.\n- Ridley Scott directed The Martian in 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
